        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1b3f414f-a8a6-52e5-b78a-62070043df5f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Leeds, Yorkshire's West Riding, West Yorkshire, England\n- Organizations: Kingdom of Elmet, Elmet\n- People: Gwallog ap Lleenog\n- Products: St John's Centre\n- Topics: History of Leeds, Brittonic kingdoms\n\nFacts:\n- In the 5th century, the name Leeds referred to a wooded area of the Kingdom of Elmet.\n- Elmet was an independent Brittonic kingdom from about the 5th century to the early 7th century in an area that later became the West Riding of Yorkshire.\n- Gwallog ap Lleenog has long been considered a probable 6th-century king of the sub-Roman state of Elmet in the Leeds area of modern Yorkshire.\n- More recent scholarship identifies Gwallog ap Lleenog more tentatively as a king of an unidentified region in the north.\n- St John's Centre is an indoor shopping centre in Leeds, West Yorkshire, England.",
